    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The acoustic emission (AE) data set is from a triaxial compression test conducted in a triaxial loading vessel equipped with a network of AE sensors . In the compression test, a cylindrical Berea sandstone specimen (diameter: 25.14 mm; length: 49.45 mm) was increasingly loaded up to failure at an axial strain rate of 1.03×10-5 /s under a constant confining pressure of 5 MPa. During the axial loading process, AE waveforms were detected by ten PZT-5A compressional crystal sensors manufactured by Boston Piezo-Optics Inc. The setup uses an Elsys acquisition system to amplify, digitize and record the waveforms, which consists of an AE-Amp Pre-amplifier (model Amp-BU-20-AE) and a High-Speed Data Acquisition (model TranNET EPC) module. We set a 40 dB pre-amplification gain and 5 kHz – 2MHz bandpass filtering. The sampling rate of waveforms was 10 MHz. The time length of each waveform was 250 μs, comprising a pre-trigger length of 50 μs and a post-trigger length of 200 μs. Here, the term “trigger” refers to one channel of the AE system being activated once the acquired waveforms meet a triggering criterion set by the user. We set the trigger level at 0.5 V and the trigger mode to use the positive slope mode. After acquiring the AE data, we manually picked the P-wave arrivals of 49,212 waveforms. To request AE waveform data, please contact Tian Yang Guo (guoty@stanford.edu) and Tiziana Vanorio (tvanorio@stanford.edu).",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Guo, T., Vanorio, T., and Ding, J. (2024). Stanford Acoustic Emission Data set. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/mz374gr4108. https://doi.org/10.25740/mz374gr4108.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
    ],
